</div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's implied that the food on the Orient Express is either made from wraiths or is a special preparation of Pathos using tempered Arcanoi (Usury, Moliate and Inhabit, perhaps). I think the latter would make more sense. Perhaps lesser plasmics could be reshaped in this way (although, I'm not sure where WTO stood on turning plasmics into anything else).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be feeding the Haighttray with the ashes of utter despair as souls warped into tobacco products are consigned to Oblivion? Seems like the kind of thing that would lead to it becoming a very powerful ashtray...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:41:53-07:00","id":891122,"title":"","content":"No not &quot;Sam haight the oblivion ruling Ash Tray!!!!! MWa ha ha hahhah ahahhah ahhha hahah aha&quot; <br /> <br /> :Gets ripoped apart by legions of haight haters, for the the idea&quot;<br /> <br /> Comes back out of his harrowing....<br /> <br /> Oh a curious question?<br /> <br /> will relic incense, or food, run out, I remember in exalted it mysticly renewed if it was a grave good, so I thought i'd ask...<br /> <br /> I could see a LOT of Spiritualists investing enough emotion in their incense for it to become a relic... and its one of the most common gravegoods...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T08:56:55-07:00","id":891174,"title":"","content":"Possibly... but would it even be a Relic? Going to someone's gravesite or an &quot;ancestor worship&quot; shrine somewhere else and burning incense seems like Memorium more than it seems like a Relic-production activity. It's the Pathos generated from the act of burning the incense, not the incense proper. It's not that this is extra special incense to which I am emotionally attached or in which I have invested a LOT of emotion. It's the catharsis, grief, filial duty, etc. of the thing. If, say, grandpa had an extra special box of really good incense that was used for such ceremonies and there was all sorts of to-do about it, then burning it might create some incense Relics. Though the emotions might have to be pretty powerful to get anything other than a minor, probably disposable Relic that made the Shadowlands smell nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a